From b2f48da0b45d6c15d52f6e9bafc30f43bf0fe6b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: box <box@localhost>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 08:44:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] service, sysext, debian: BengalOS layout without sudo
 (draft)

fp5-qtee.socket (Accept=yes, MaxConnections=1) starts
fp5-qtee-session@.service, whose broker reads one MODE line, checks the
peer with SO_PEERCRED + pkcheck (org.fp5.qtee.{unlock,list,manage}) and
execs the session on the socket. User unit for the watcher, polkit
policy, presets, sysext build script (erofs), debian/ skeleton, and
docs/bengalos-mbn.md. Not tested on the phone.
